# Mobile update workflow (fast track)

When finishing work that touches `mobile/`, build **live release APK(s) only** for the app(s) that actually changed. Do not skip unless the user explicitly says so.

## Scope — which APK(s)

| What changed | Build |
|---|---|
| `mobile/apps/driver/**` only | `can-go-driver-release.apk` only |
| `mobile/apps/passenger/**` only | `can-go-passenger-release.apk` only |
| Shared (`mobile/packages/**`, both apps, Android shared) | Both release APKs |
| Backend / admin / web only (no `mobile/` edits) | Skip |

Never build local/LAN APKs (`*-local.apk`) unless the user explicitly asks.

## Do NOT do (unless user asks)

- Localhost / web-server preview
- Cursor IDE browser refresh / screenshots
- Passenger APK when only driver changed (and vice versa)
- Local API APKs (`CANGO_API_BASE=http://…`)

## Build + install

ADB: `D:\Android\Sdk\platform-tools\adb.exe` (or `$env:LOCALAPPDATA\Android\Sdk\platform-tools\adb.exe`).

Build **one APK at a time**. Do not run `gradlew --stop` or kill Java/Dart while a build is running.

```powershell
$adb = "D:\Android\Sdk\platform-tools\adb.exe"
if (-not (Test-Path $adb)) { $adb = "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\Android\Sdk\platform-tools\adb.exe" }
$liveApi = "https://www.can-rides.ca/api"
$apks = "d:\xampp\htdocs\get-transfer\mobile\apks"
New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $apks | Out-Null

# Driver release (only if driver or shared changed)
cd "d:\xampp\htdocs\get-transfer\mobile\apps\driver"
flutter build apk --release --dart-define=CANGO_API_BASE=$liveApi
Copy-Item "build\app\outputs\flutter-apk\app-release.apk" "$apks\can-go-driver-release.apk" -Force

# Passenger release (only if passenger or shared changed)
cd "d:\xampp\htdocs\get-transfer\mobile\apps\passenger"
flutter build apk --release --dart-define=CANGO_API_BASE=$liveApi
Copy-Item "build\app\outputs\flutter-apk\app-release.apk" "$apks\can-go-passenger-release.apk" -Force

# Install on phone if connected (release only)
& $adb devices -l
# adb -s <serial> install -r "$apks\can-go-driver-release.apk"
# adb -s <serial> install -r "$apks\can-go-passenger-release.apk"
```

Tell the user which release APK path(s) were built and whether install succeeded (or that no device was connected).
